Dear Roudha & All,



Thanks for the initial meeting.

Below are the questions I mentioned:

What and why:

What problem do they want to solve? Is it duplicate data entry, reporting, =
auditing, or something else?

What data needs to flow? For example, work orders, maintenance schedules, o=
perating hours/counters, spare parts/inventory, costs, or completion report=
s.

Should data flow one way or both ways? Which system is the "master" for whi=
ch data?



The Oracle side:

Which Oracle product do they use (Fusion Cloud, E-Business Suite, JD Edward=
s, EAM, etc.), and does it run in the cloud or on-premises?

Do they have an integration platform (e.g., Oracle Integration Cloud) and a=
n in-house integration team, or do they expect us to handle everything?

Do they expect us to provide an API for them to call, or for us to write da=
ta directly into their system?



Operations and security:

How often must data be synchronized: in real-time, hourly, or daily?

Where does their maintenance software run, and does it have network access =
to their IT environment? What are the IT security requirements (VPN, authen=
tication, firewall)?

Do they have a test environment we can use?



Scope:

How many facilities/assets and approximately how many components are involv=
ed?

When do they need this, and is it part of an existing contract or a new add=
-on?

Who is the technical contact on the Oracle side, and can they provide docum=
entation on their data model/API?





With a response to all the above it would be possible for our Software desi=
gner to provide a time/estimate for cost in hours for implementation.



Who from DMC will be the technical responsible for this integration ?



Below is the link to the snaggit page containing the API parameters/informa=
tion:

https://mm-mobile-api-dev.azurewebsites.net/swagger/index.html?urls.primary=
Name=3DVIEW%20MAINTENANCE%20API%20V1



Thanks & best regards,



